    "created_at": "2018-08-03T14:49:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-03T14:49:09Z",
    "body": "Hmm, I think the intent was to replace just 3.7... E.g. type conversions should still happen and such. This just further makes the OP's case, of course :).\r\n\r\nThe following would the plan for attributes:\r\n\r\n- The [general section on attributes](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#idl-attributes) should state that describing an attribute should be accompanied by getting and (if appropriate) setting steps. I.e. it defines the terms \"getting steps\" and \"setting steps\", and even gives some guidance on how to state them (Currently we say things like \"On getting, ...\" \"On setting to value _v_, ...\"). I believe there is an existing Web IDL issue about this but I can't find it at the moment.\r\n- Also mention that certain extended attributes may modify the getting steps and setting steps?\r\n- Update the ES binding section to explicitly execute the getting/setting steps.\r\n- Update [CEReactions] to specifically replace the getting/setting steps, and call into the \"old\" getting/setting steps.\r\n\r\nAnd we'd do something similar for the other (non-attribute) constructs.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
